  "question": {
    "text": "A cube of mass <math><mi>m</mi></math> is placed on top of a wedge of mass <math><mn>2</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>m</mi></math>, as shown in figure. There is no friction between the cube and the wedge. The minimum co-efficient of friction between the wedge and the horizontal surface, so that the wedge does not move is<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0024_04905ffbf75e.png\" style=\"width: 174px; height: 118px;\" />"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>0.1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>0.2</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>0.3</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The normal reaction between the wedge and the block is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>N</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></math></p><p>So the net horizontal force on the wedge is<br /><br /><math><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mrow></math><br /><br />The normal reaction between the wedge and the ground is</p><p><math><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mrow></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>&#952;</mi></math><br /><br />Now,&nbsp;<math><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mi>N</mi></math> gives<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>F</mi><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>cos</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mi>&#952;</mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br />For&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>45</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.</mn><mn>2</mn></math></p>"
  }
}